  {
    "sha": "b3de18494af0b5f856299af5197dc39477d87ee5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGIzZGUxODQ5NGFmMGI1Zjg1NjI5OWFmNTE5N2RjMzk0NzdkODdlZTU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T20:21:38Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T20:21:38Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(setup): refuse generation under a WCS tilted off the machine Z\n\nA milling setup's WCS could be turned onto another face, but every\nmilling generator cuts along the machine's Z, so the toolpath machined\nthe part as it lies (the wrong face) and reported OK; only the post's\nrotated-offset clause (#315) held it back. Generation now refuses a WCS\nwhose Z is tilted off the machine's, by name, pointing at the setup's\nPart alignment, and a facing pick on a face that is level only in the\ntilted WCS says the WCS is why. A WCS turned only about Z still\ngenerates.\n\nFixes #1510\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
